        "relationship_type": "related",
        "body": "連用形 is a more formal way to connect phrases or clauses, often used in writing. It shares the same basic meaning as the て form. In the case of ではなくて・じゃなくて, the 連用形 becomes ではなく・じゃなく, e.g. 病院ではなく、図書館です 'It's not a hospital, but a library.' (Same meaning, just more formal in tone.)",
